As a Resident Evil fan, with Resident Evil 4 my favourite from the series and Resident evil 7 as my second one, I am writing this review too tell you that Village became my second favourite from the series. Alot of Resident Evil 4 vibes combined with Resident Evil 7 gameplay, you get too play the Village mission from Resident Evil 4 when the bell rings, ironic, isn't it ? 
It is a game that you can't stop at just only one playthough, now that I unlocked the last difficulty, i will start my second one :). Maybe we will get some DLCs too continue the story.

Pros:
-good visual design, audio was great too, sometimes nothing was happening and it was still a bit scary;
-good inventory future, updated the one from Resident Evil 4, the merchant from RE4 is back too :D;
-best creature and monsters design by far compared too last RE games, Resident Evil 7 was lazy at this point;
-good story telling, some good plot twists;
-that thick white dress man;
-by living in Romania, it gave me goosebumps too see the name of the creatures: Vârcolac, Soldat, Moroiaică, etc.;

Cons:
-nearly the end, the game becomes a bit first person shooter and less horror genre;
-this game was less scarier, compared to Resident Evil 7, i wanted too poop my pants but no luck :(;
-the field of view sucks and it's no setting to change that, but it makes you feel more unsafe when checking corners :D;
-kind of a short story, 08 hours for me, and I admired the visuals and looted nearly everything possible.


Bonus:
(maybe Spoiler) When I reached the stronghold, it gave me some vibes of The Evil Within, i don't know if it was intentionally or not, but it was cool :D.

SERIOUS TIME;

