For someone who loves horror and enjoys the Resident Evil games, I have to say that Village is an amazing entry to the franchise. Besides Village I have only played RE1 (Remastered), RE7, and the remakes of RE2 and RE3. If you like a lot of action, exploration, and crafting you will love this game. If you are more of a horror fan, unfortunately you may be disappointed. While there are a couple jumpscares and creepy moments throughout the game, the game itself is not that scary. However, if you are like myself and you appreciate graphics, ambience, and the artistic design of games, you will be blown away. There wasn't a single moment I wasn't wowed by the designs of the environments and enemies.

Before I finished the game I read a few non-spoiler reviews. One of these reviews pointed out that each section of the game is very unique and feels awkwardly connected. And after playing Village I totally agree. With each area you visit to defeat the four lords, it seems as if each area was designed by different teams. And once the game was finished, they tried their best to connect them together. Don't get me wrong. Each of these areas were a blast to explore (the castle section was my favorite), but none of them felt related to each other at all. This is pretty much my only major complaint with the game.

{ Rating: 7/10 }

Look the plot is really Bonkers;
The music is marvellous;
The characters..... have marvellous designs but become kinda.... edgy in terms of personnality;
And the gameplay is magnificent, till you reach the endgame.

It grabbed the good of the classics, but unfortenatly it also grabbed the awfullness of the later entries. It's a good game, but it's plot twists altough mildly interesting are nothing out of this world.

I want to forget I played this just so I can play it again.

I agree with the people who say it's more action than 7 but scarier than 4. But I also have something else to say;

I finished it, and I felt the same sensation I felt when finishing a BioShock game. And honestly? That's great. This game is great. I can't wait for RE9.

There are two things you learn after completing this game;

1. This is a story about family, which is what makes it so powerful.

2. You are the true monster for hunting those poor animals.

Let's see here. Horror aspect from RE7 combined with the action and setting from RE4? Sign me the f up. Story and gameplay is the same as you would expect from the Resident Evil franchise, so no faults there. Good thing the places you visited in the village and castle demos just about scratch the surface, so they didn't go overboard there.

There's a few things I'd like to see fixed for the pc version:
-fov slider (especially for us ultrawide monitor users);
-drag and drop inventory management (iirc RE2 remake does have this);
-please fix the mouse sensivity. I had to put it at maximum for it to feal normal without changing my DPI settings.

I recommend you wait a bit to buy this game until these points are fixed. But if you really can't wait, I'd say have fun!
